 #uuid "3ebe5d30-e92e-5943-8471-f25c505f78bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512005} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd1710b-9b32-522b-9601-eba847c1e078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ebe5d30-e92e-5943-8471-f25c505f78bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512005} :answer-field/id #uuid "fee93e3b-06c8-5ee1-8dd8-365bfe5b8c36" :answer-field/key "The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4ce2ea85-552c-5e62-a3ef-0a5e7f4819be" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186512034 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80ec998e-ebc7-57cf-9585-e7037333b8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512039} {:answer/id #uuid "89c1df3f-3762-583b-8c83-ee434a3252d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89c1df3f-3762-583b-8c83-ee434a3252d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512041} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f8b1ab-556a-50ab-8924-407cb71a9248" :answer-field/key "The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3e3065-d748-56e4-9ea7-63e3f483a888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512004} {:answer/id #uuid "8a49b2d2-e020-53df-a5ee-1f419297d7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a49b2d2-e020-53df-a5ee-1f419297d7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512043} :answer-field/id #uuid "98c2438b-478a-5125-9517-0d2f3e092a73" :answer-field/key "The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=2n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512048} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20cc89a1-3922-5c45-a9fa-d75c8e199080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511993} {:answer/id #uuid "a40ec01a-5ba0-5a70-b087-12eb7c43c39f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20cc89a1-3922-5c45-a9fa-d75c8e199080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511993} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac436c36-bf17-5a14-b653-d165723d782d" :answer-field/key "The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c7e38f3-2c78-5b87-9a78-4823ef519ba4" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=2n\\pi.$” is false. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d6f79e7-d13c-5f7a-b9cc-99ef5cb21c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513213} {:answer/id #uuid "d0288b28-716e-53ef-8dbf-a2ba80199026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d6f79e7-d13c-5f7a-b9cc-99ef5cb21c8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513213} :answer-field/id #uuid "b03c65b1-930b-5ed0-9553-a0f24170a0dc" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513217} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed6cc88f-4f54-5e0f-bb09-f0c4681c465c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513238} {:answer/id #uuid "eecaf378-e97c-5950-84b6-d7499a11193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eecaf378-e97c-5950-84b6-d7499a11193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513239} :answer-field/id #uuid "db77d2f4-c1af-5a32-947d-6b6feb9c3a86" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [0,\\infty)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4971a396-3d1e-5545-a13a-e2c55f7f04f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513199} {:answer/id #uuid "db96268f-2e77-5e10-a9ad-ede7332fa428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db96268f-2e77-5e10-a9ad-ede7332fa428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513232} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcffd72-6dc0-5541-bf1e-4be85e0bd14d" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "55cecc39-f460-5ecf-abe4-4ef195040d31" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it is one-to-one on that interval.\n\nThe function is constant: distinct inputs in each listed interval have the same output $2$. Thus it is not one-to-one on any of the three intervals.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of these intervals\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029905eb-f32e-56f7-816a-edf98d09bd33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516988} {:answer/id #uuid "d768524b-3951-56ce-a481-d434e040922c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d768524b-3951-56ce-a481-d434e040922c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517077} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ad04f2-c4c7-5b44-a3d0-f1d268d4ff9a" :answer-field/key "$x=-2\\pi $ is in the domain." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "431adfeb-59b2-56c6-a267-16169be9fc4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517016} {:answer/id #uuid "b94767de-c850-5fe3-bf49-5fba9d4a267d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b94767de-c850-5fe3-bf49-5fba9d4a267d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517066} :answer-field/id #uuid "d19e0a8e-32b2-58e2-bea4-5fa816f4b8da" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517075} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "872443e8-aa3d-5ae6-b536-76504b4e9cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517049} {:answer/id #uuid "fd678153-1542-56a0-a47d-f42aa825b0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd678153-1542-56a0-a47d-f42aa825b0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517096} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebcdc48f-6769-579c-91a1-4be4d960be47" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6cb9d51c-3919-54db-9e0b-8f7841c0c2b7" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ therefore the function doesn't have a maximum value. Hence, statements “The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1].$” and “$y=-1$ is the maximum value of the function” are both false.\n\n- The function's domain is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement “$x=-2\\pi $ is in the domain” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f457bc94-632a-5352-992e-e6c5a3424593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519908} {:answer/id #uuid "f9239b0b-9b82-5bd6-9884-9a3032281b92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f457bc94-632a-5352-992e-e6c5a3424593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519908} :answer-field/id #uuid "085ba0ab-a4e5-5515-bf9d-4e1c2f9bf259" :answer-field/key "$y' + 2 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f2ab4bd-2b5e-5363-b5dc-1ad703f3184a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519863} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa54f6-1e4d-5baf-bb5e-f802dd30bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa54f6-1e4d-5baf-bb5e-f802dd30bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519898} :answer-field/id #uuid "1726f0ce-5eb4-5ac5-b540-d18d2403b11c" :answer-field/key "$yy' - 5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = x^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b3bc395-fe4c-526e-b802-660027798152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519865} {:answer/id #uuid "ec30e286-0384-5a12-9d88-b913c676a26b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec30e286-0384-5a12-9d88-b913c676a26b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519905} :answer-field/id #uuid "aecef73e-7b03-515d-8ed8-0ba8a0e9f3b8" :answer-field/key "$y^{2}y' - x \\cdot y^{5} = 4 \\cdot y^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41658dd9-b512-54b4-8eaf-1cd8fd36a4fa" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y^{2}y' - x \\cdot y^{5} = 4 \\cdot y^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - x \\cdot y^{3} = 4 \\cdot y^{2}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $yy' - 5 \\cdot x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = x^{2}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - \\frac{5 \\cdot x}{\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{x^{2}}{y}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y' + 2 \\cdot y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\nTherefore, select none of the given equations."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eef27d2b-6149-5070-b711-f4dcc7db2a03" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Bernoulli Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9856cd8f-1ecf-5090-b104-4a61b05f6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519882} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd67961-35d9-52b9-9614-7f044b5e3dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9856cd8f-1ecf-5090-b104-4a61b05f6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519882} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d67a8e9-5e92-5864-884f-542d26df09cc" :answer-field/key "$y' + y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "746f231b-c31e-52ec-8372-86806f91864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519872} {:answer/id #uuid "a833f96f-7658-5c7e-872d-a2f9dcb8e16b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746f231b-c31e-52ec-8372-86806f91864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519872} :answer-field/id #uuid "606f37f2-ccbf-570a-be0c-306b515b0fbb" :answer-field/key "$y^{2}y' - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{5} = 2 \\cdot y^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519867} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad9b1b8-d78d-53c9-918c-c359a0595b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519850} {:answer/id #uuid "8817770a-e70f-55cc-a160-cc3388ebb793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ad9b1b8-d78d-53c9-918c-c359a0595b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519850} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec85d78e-46bb-5696-9523-555403cf0e24" :answer-field/key "$yy' - x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = 5 \\cdot x^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae013de7-6f4e-5b96-9f10-eb4987b6f88b" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a Bernoulli differential equation?\n\nWork on intervals where $x>0$ and $y>0$, and where the displayed coefficients are defined.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A Bernoulli differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny'+p(x)y=q(x)y^n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options. Work on the stated positive domain, so dividing by powers of $y$ is valid.\n\n- Equation $y^{2}y' - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{5} = 2 \\cdot y^{4}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y^{2}$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot y^{3} = 2 \\cdot y^{2}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $yy' - x \\cdot \\sqrt{y} = 5 \\cdot x^{2}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. Dividing by $y$, we get\n\n$$\ny' - \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot x^{2}}{y}\n$$\n\n The normalized equation contains two different powers of $y$, neither with exponent 1.\n\n- Equation $y' + y \\cdot \\log{\\left(x \\right)} = 2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\log{\\left(y \\right)}$ is *not* a Bernoulli differential equation. The normalized equation contains a function of $y$ that is not a single power of $y$.\n\nTherefore, select none of the given equations."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0184f2ee-4e64-5c2a-