e/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624672} :answer-field/id #uuid "90ecb2e1-2546-569b-9b7f-8227f1992d76" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbb{Z}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e7f7e59-12b8-5d8f-a27b-48f0bd02db19" :question/problem "To which of the following sets do all the real numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We must check whether each set contains all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{N}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. For instance, $\\frac{1}{2}$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Z}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ contains the negative rational numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. For instance, $1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the real numbers.\n\nTherefore, select none of the sets; leave every box unchecked."}]
